# =============================================================================
# MANUSCRIPT/ (Nature Energy + Applied Energy versions)
# Source (.tex / .bib / .cls / .sty / .bst) and figure assets ARE tracked;
# compiled PDFs and tooling caches are NOT — recompile from source. Globals
# above cover most LaTeX intermediates; below adds per-folder tool caches.
# =============================================================================
MANUSCRIPT/**/main.pdf
MANUSCRIPT/**/_minted-*/
MANUSCRIPT/**/svg-inkscape/
MANUSCRIPT/**/.texpadtmp/
MANUSCRIPT/**/.latexmk/

# Gurobi
gurobi.log

# Documentation (except README.md)
docs/

# =============================================================================
# Data tiering (see data/README.md "How to get the data")
# =============================================================================
# Tier 1 (TRACKED in git): YAMLs + scripts + perf curves + small bridge CSVs +
#   docs + tiny summary CSVs + the eleven 8760-h model-input CSVs that
#   src/data.py reads (DAM LMP, ambient, carbon intensity, the 60u workload
#   aggregate, Henry Hub daily; ~6 MB). A fresh clone runs every case and the
#   test suite with no data step.
#
# Tier 2 (IGNORED — regen via `make data`, ~10 min): the remaining bulk ERCOT
#   downloads, full Open-Meteo exports, non-baseline workload variants and
#   intermediate raw files.
#
# Tier 3 (IGNORED — manual download per data/MANUAL_COLLECTION.md): NLR 1 GB
#   raw 1-minute AI workload profiles (third-party data, not redistributable).
# =============================================================================

# Tier 2 — ERCOT historical (regen: data/_raw/fetch_ercot_dam.py + _rtm.py + _eia930_erco.py)
data/ercot/*_dam_spp_all.csv.gz
data/ercot/*_rtm_spp_all.csv.gz
data/ercot/*_rtm_lmp_houston_hourly.csv
data/ercot/*_eia930_erco_full.csv
data/ercot/*_genmix_erco.csv
data/ercot/*_load_system_actual.csv

# Tier 2 — Weather (regen: data/_raw/fetch_open_meteo_houston.py)
data/weather/houston_hourly_*.csv
data/weather/houston_wet_bulb_combined.csv

# Tier 2 — Hourly carbon intensity (regen: data/_raw/build_real_carbon_intensity.py)

# Tier 2 — Workload aggregates (regen: data/_raw/build_real_ai_workload.py, requires Tier 3 input)
data/workload/dc_200mw_real_*u_*.csv
!data/workload/dc_200mw_real_60u_2018.csv
data/workload/cooling_load_pue*.csv

# Tier 2 — Henry Hub daily (regen: data/_raw/fetch_henry_hub.py)
data/economics/henry_hub_monthly_summary.csv

# Tier 2 — Intermediate raw downloads (regenerable, large)
data/_raw/*.xls
data/_raw/*.log
data/_raw/EIA930_BALANCE_*.csv
data/_raw/ai_workload_dataset.zip
data/_raw/nlr_extract/

# Tier 3 — NLR raw 1-minute profiles (manual download, 226 MB, third-party)
data/workload/raw_nlr_colocation/*.csv

# =============================================================================
# submission_audit/ — pre-submission run-and-backfill audit (2026-07-26)
# Tracked: the report, the merged results.json with per-number provenance, the
# unrounded 100-run ledger, the Supplementary Note 7 draft and its source list,
# the re-runnable driver scripts and the revised Figure 6. Not tracked: the
# per-run solve artifacts of the 85 new runs (~28 MB), regenerable with
# submission_audit/scripts/run_gate.py, run_b1.py and run_b2.py — same policy
# as outputs/ above.
# =============================================================================
submission_audit/runs_gate/
submission_audit/runs_b1/
submission_audit/runs_b2/
# Colour-vision simulations are QA by-products, regenerable from the tracked PNG.
submission_audit/figures/*_protan.png
submission_audit/figures/*_deuter.png
submission_audit/figures/*_tritan.png
